{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Planarity\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/Planarity\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/Planarity\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/Planarity\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Planarity\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PlanarEmbedding","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A self-loop appears twice in its vertex’s order, its two ends adjacent, enclosing a face of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"length 1. Parallel copies sit side by side, each consecutive pair enclosing a face of length 2.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Each clockwise order starts at the first edge of ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdges(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Faces.","type":"text"}]},{"text":" The face after the half-edge from u along edge e to w continues with the half-edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"before e in the clockwise order at w (NetworkX’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"next_face_half_edge"},{"text":"), so a face lies to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"right of each of its half-edges. Faces are counted per connected component, and an isolated","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex has none: two disjoint triangles have four faces.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The embedding keeps the graph it was made from (copy-on-write, so O(1)); mutating the graph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"afterwards does not change it. When a graph has several embeddings, which one is returned is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not specified, but it depends only on the graph’s rows: graphs with the same vertices, the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge positions and the same incidence order get the same embedding."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Planarity"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PlanarEmbedding"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:9Planarity15PlanarEmbeddingV","symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PlanarEmbedding","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding.swift#L63","fileName":"PlanarEmbedding.swift"},"roleHeading":"Structure","title":"PlanarEmbedding"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/planarity\/planarembedding"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A planar embedding of a graph: a rotation system, the clockwise order of the edges around each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex, over every edge position (NetworkX’s "},{"code":"PlanarEmbedding","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", LEMON’s "},{"code":"PlanarEmbedding","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"OGDF’s "},{"code":"CombinatorialEm